The contracts are permissive on purpose. They are a small, reusable escrow
pattern, and the Ergo ecosystem is better off being able to copy them without
conditions. The application is AGPL because it is a website: anyone may run
their own instance, and anyone who modifies it and serves it to others has to
publish those modifications.


WHAT IS NOT COVERED BY EITHER LICENCE
─────────────────────────────────────

The artwork of Ergo Champions, Ergo Mummy and Mage Champions is NOT ours and is
NOT licensed by this repository.

It is hosted with the written permission of the collection owner, for the sole
purpose of serving it on this marketplace. That permission is to display the
work. It is not permission for anyone else to copy, redistribute or relicense
it, and nothing in the LICENSE files above should be read as granting that.

For this reason the image files are deliberately excluded from the repository
(see .gitignore). They are uploaded straight to the host at deploy time and
never enter git history — so that the permission remains something the owner
can withdraw, rather than something published irrevocably.

Anyone running their own instance needs their own arrangement with the
collection owner, or should serve the artwork from IPFS, which is where it
canonically lives. Every token's on-chain R9 register holds that address and R8
holds the SHA-256 of the file, so an IPFS-only instance is fully functional and
verifiable.

The collection metadata in data/ is derived from the Ergo blockchain: token
ids, issuer addresses, trait values, and the burn audit. The facts are public
records. The trait names and descriptions originate with the collection
authors and are reproduced here only to identify their tokens.

The interface sprites in public/ui/ are cut from the author's own game and are
covered by the AGPL like the rest of the application.
